<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE topic SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       id="install" title="Install">

    <show-structure for="chapter,procedure" depth="2"/>

    <tldr>
        <p>Compiled for JDK %jdk%. The plugin needs Maven %maven%.</p>
    </tldr>

    <p>
        Add this to the pom of the module that holds your weave. <code>mvn verify</code> then
        weaves its classes as part of the build.
    </p>

    <code-block lang="xml"><![CDATA[
<properties>
    <maven.compiler.release>%jdk%</maven.compiler.release>
    <aether.weaver.version>%version%</aether.weaver.version>
</properties>

<dependencyManagement>
    <dependencies>
        <dependency>
            <groupId>%group%</groupId>
            <artifactId>aether-weaver-bom</artifactId>
            <version>${aether.weaver.version}</version>
            <type>pom</type>
            <scope>import</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>
</dependencyManagement>

<dependencies>
    <dependency>
        <groupId>%group%</groupId>
        <artifactId>aether-weaver-api</artifactId>
    </dependency>
    <dependency>
        <groupId>%group%</groupId>
        <artifactId>aether-weaver-processor</artifactId>
        <scope>provided</scope>
    </dependency>
</dependencies>

<build>
    <plugins>
        <plugin>
            <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
            <artifactId>maven-compiler-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>%compiler-plugin%</version>
            <configuration>
                <proc>full</proc>
            </configuration>
        </plugin>
        <plugin>
            <groupId>%group%</groupId>
            <artifactId>aether-weaver-maven-plugin</artifactId>
            <version>${aether.weaver.version}</version>
            <executions>
                <execution>
                    <goals>
                        <goal>weave</goal>
                    </goals>
                </execution>
            </executions>
        </plugin>
    </plugins>
</build>
]]></code-block>

    <chapter title="What each part is for" id="parts">
        <deflist type="medium">
            <def title="aether-weaver-bom">
                <p>
                    Imported, so the dependencies under it carry no <code>version</code>. A
                    <code>&lt;plugin&gt;</code> takes none of that, which is why the plugin's own
                    version is written out.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="aether-weaver-api">
                <p>
                    The annotations and the selector grammar you write a weave with. Its
                    transitive closure is empty, so it adds nothing else to your classpath.
                    <a href="what-is-aether-weaver.topic">What Aether Weaver is</a> shows what a
                    weave looks like.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="aether-weaver-processor">
                <p>
                    Checks every weave while <code>javac</code> runs and records it. At
                    <code>provided</code> scope it stays out of the artifact you publish.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="aether-weaver-maven-plugin">
                <p>
                    Its <code>weave</code> goal binds to <code>process-classes</code> and rewrites
                    your output directory in place. <a href="maven-goals.topic">The plugin reference</a>
                    has the goals and their parameters.
                </p>
            </def>
            <def title="proc full">
                <p>
                    Since JDK 21, <code>javac</code> does not run a classpath annotation processor
                    unless asked. Without this setting the processor never runs.
                </p>
            </def>
        </deflist>
    </chapter>

    <procedure title="Weave a module" id="run">
        <step>
            <p>Put the block above into your pom, and write a weave beside the classes it
                changes. <a href="first-weave.topic">Your first weave</a> is three short classes.</p>
        </step>
        <step>
            <p>Compile and weave. The plugin runs after <code>compile</code>, over the classes
                javac wrote.</p>
            <code-block lang="bash">
mvn verify
            </code-block>
        </step>
        <step>
            <p>Read the plugin's closing line. It counts the weaves it loaded and the classes it
                rewrote.</p>
            <code-block lang="console">
[INFO] Aether Weaver: 1 weave, 1 class rewritten (main).
            </code-block>
        </step>
    </procedure>

    <tip>
        <p>
            Maven resolves these artifacts from the repositories you have configured. To build
            them yourself, clone <code>%repo%.git</code> and run <code>mvn install</code>. Set
            <code>aether.weaver.version</code> to whatever the branch you checked out declares
            — <a href="building-and-testing.topic">Building and testing</a> covers the branches.
        </p>
    </tip>

    <chapter title="When that line never appears" id="silent">
        <p>
            The plugin finds your weaves through one file, and the processor is what writes it.
            <a href="weave-discovery.topic">How a weave is found</a> has the rest of that path.
        </p>

        <code-block lang="mermaid">
flowchart TB
    S["Your sources"] --> J["javac, with proc full"]
    J --> M["META-INF/aether/weaves.json"]
    J --> K["Compiled classes"]
    M --> G["The weave goal, at process-classes"]
    K --> G
    G --> O["Rewritten bytecode, same directory"]
        </code-block>

        <warning>
            <p>
                A build with the plugin and no processor stays green and weaves none of its own
                classes. If the closing line is missing, check that <code>proc</code> is
                <code>full</code> and that <code>aether-weaver-processor</code> is on the compile
                classpath.
            </p>
        </warning>

        <note>
            <p>
                A manifest that exists but cannot be read is <code>AW2300</code>: delete
                <code>target/classes</code> and compile again. <a href="diagnostics.topic">Diagnostics</a>
                explains what a code is telling you.
            </p>
        </note>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="The artifacts for the other drivers" id="drivers">
        <p>
            Three more exist, one for each of the other drivers.
            <a href="artifacts.topic">Artefacts and modules</a> has the full list.
        </p>
    </chapter>

